    "opening": "Product costs are assigned to inventory and generally become cost of goods sold when the related goods are sold. Period costs, such as selling and administrative costs, are recognized in the relevant period. Whether a cost is fixed or variable is a separate question.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>Product costs are assigned to inventory and generally become cost of goods sold when the related goods are sold. Period costs, such as selling and administrative costs, are recognized in the relevant period. Whether a cost is fixed or variable is a separate question.</p>",
