    "id": "N051",
    "slug": "payback-period",
    "title": "Payback Period: Cash Recovery and Its Limits",
    "seoTitle": "Payback Period: Formula and Uneven Cash Flows",
    "description": "Calculate payback for equal and uneven cash flows, handle partial years and end-year timing, and compare discounted recovery with the limits of simple payback.",
    "metaDescription": "Calculate payback for equal and uneven cash flows, handle partial years and end-year timing, and compare discounted recovery with the limits of simple payback.",
    "primaryKeyword": "payback period",
    "scopeBoundary": "Investment cash recovery; not the cleaning-specific acquisition-payback or full capital-budgeting selection guide.",
    "opening": "The payback period is the time forecast net cash inflows take to recover an initial investment. For equal positive annual flows, divide the outlay by annual net cash inflow. For uneven flows, use a cumulative schedule; fractional years require an explicit within-year timing assumption.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>The payback period is the time forecast net cash inflows take to recover an initial investment. For equal positive annual flows, divide the outlay by annual net cash inflow. For uneven flows, use a cumulative schedule; fractional years require an explicit within-year timing assumption.</p>",
